# SDD product law and release gates are repository truth (canon v6, T-050-06A /
# SPEC A1.7 / V21). The original shape here was a catch-all deny (/specs/*) plus a
# narrow per-artifact-extension opt-in — NINE registered bug instances (the
# gitignore-verdict-evidence-untrackable-fourth-recurrence class and its siblings:
# ALPHA-*-QA.md, PRE-PR-REVIEW.md, reviews/, verdicts/, remote-bugs-gitignore-
# blocks-new-intake, ...) proved that shape was ITSELF the defect: every new canon
# artifact class needed its own whitelist line, or it was silently born untracked,
# unreviewable, and invisible to the push-time range-scoped denylist scan.
# specs/releases/** inverted this once already; FR1/T-050-06A widens the SAME
# inversion to every other canon area this release creates or moves — audits/,
# ADRs/, bugs/_archive/, backlog/_archive/, releases/_archive/, and root _archive/
# (still on disk until T-050-14 retires it; kept fully tracked in the meantime,
# never silently re-ignored). This IS the deliberate privacy decision, stated once:
# the catch-all backstop is replaced by explicit per-area opt-in (every canon path
# TRACKED BY DEFAULT) plus the push-time denylist scan, which is the boundary that
# actually holds. Only the narrow scratch/private-notes class the original
# catch-all ever actually hid (local-notes.md, tmp/ working dirs — see
# test_source_repo_hygiene.py) still gets denied, per area. No future canonical
# artifact class (this release's or any later one's) ever needs a new whitelist
# line for content already inside one of the areas below.
#
# The three FR1/FR6 orphans of the OLD shape are deleted outright, not widened:
# specs/assets/ (retired into memory/ARCHITECTURE.md, T-050-06) and
# specs/backlog/remote-bugs/ (retired, T-050-06 — "dies with the folder", FR1;
# tests/integration/test_governance_intake_not_gitignored.py's remote-bugs
# coverage retires with it, same commit) no longer exist on disk at all. Root
# specs/_archive/ is NOT an orphan in the same sense — it still holds real,
# committed history until T-050-14 repoints the FROZEN gate class — so its narrow
# releases-only opt-in is replaced by the same full per-area inversion below,
# never left without one.
/specs/*
!/specs/constitution.md
!/specs/memory/
!/specs/memory/**
!/specs/audits/
!/specs/audits/**
!/specs/ADRs/
!/specs/ADRs/**
# Bug records are repository truth (bug-registration-guardrail mandates
# registration in specs/bugs/ with redacted content). Top-level bugs/ stays a
# narrow *.md/*.jsonl opt-in (covers BUGS.jsonl + AGENTS.md); _archive/ is fully
# tracked (widened from *.md-only — bugs_histo.jsonl and any other archived
# artifact type must be visible too).
!/specs/bugs/
/specs/bugs/*
!/specs/bugs/*.md
!/specs/bugs/*.jsonl
!/specs/bugs/_archive/
!/specs/bugs/_archive/**
# Backlog is PM-curated repository truth (backlog-ownership + release-governance;
# v0.1.49 FR1). Top-level backlog/ stays a narrow *.md opt-in; _archive/ is fully
# tracked (widened from *.md-only, same reason as bugs/_archive/ above).
!/specs/backlog/
/specs/backlog/*
!/specs/backlog/*.md
!/specs/backlog/_archive/
!/specs/backlog/_archive/**
!/specs/releases/
!/specs/releases/**
/specs/releases/**/local-notes.md
/specs/releases/**/tmp/
!/specs/releases/_archive/**
!/specs/_archive/
!/specs/_archive/**
/specs/_archive/**/local-notes.md

# Operator private working draft — never commit
docs/00_medium_mine.md

# specs-evolution migration backups (FR-S04) — never tracked
specs_bkp/
**/specs_bkp/
